message: "If you use this workflow design or software in research, please cite it using this metadata. Citation is appreciated and does not add conditions to the MIT License."
type: software
title: "MedChem Human Loop: Traceable Evidence for Human-Guided Molecular Optimization"
authors:
  - name: "whlym"
abstract: "A human-in-the-loop molecular optimization workflow design, auditable OpenMM execution and trajectory analysis utilities, an optional fixed-pose scoring and pretrained ADMET-AI reference interface, and a synthetic evidence assembly example. Planned components include a medicinal-chemistry case library, local molecular edits, and constrained diffusion; the release is not a trained reinforcement-learning or autonomous drug-discovery system. Author mark: whlym. Developed with AI assistance."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/whlym248/medchem-human-loop"
url: "https://github.com/whlym248/medchem-human-loop"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - medicinal chemistry
  - human-in-the-loop
  - molecular dynamics
  - evidence provenance
  - molecular optimization
